# Grainlet overview

Import **only** from the listed subpaths. Never pull route/forms/auth/auth-sdk/i18n/query/store/ssr/testing/devtools/utils from `grainlet`.

| Import from | Typical APIs |
|-------------|--------------|
| `grainlet` | signals, `render`/`hydrate`, `Show`/`For`/`Suspense`, `createResource`/`lazy` |
| `grainlet/route` | `Router`/`Route`/`Link`/`navigate`/`useParams` |
| `grainlet/forms` | `FormProvider`/`Field`/`rules`/`required` |
| `grainlet/auth` | `createAuth`/`AuthProvider`/`useSession`/`ProtectedRoute` |
| `grainlet/auth-sdk` | `getGoogleIdToken`/`GoogleSignIn`/`createAuthSdk` |
| `grainlet/i18n` | `createI18n`/`I18nProvider`/`useTranslation` |
| `grainlet/query` | `QueryClient`/`useQuery`/`useMutation` |
| `grainlet/store` | `createStore`/`produce`/`reconcile` |
| `grainlet/utils` | path/object/guards/async helpers |
| `grainlet/ssr` | `renderToString*`/`Head`/`createNodeHandler` |
| `grainlet/testing` | `render`/`screen`/`fireEvent`/`waitFor` |
| `grainlet/devtools` | `installDevtoolsHook`/`GrainletDevtools` |

Provider order: **Auth → I18n → Query → Router**.

```js
// Good
import { createSignal, Show } from 'grainlet';
import { useSession } from 'grainlet/auth';
import { useQuery } from 'grainlet/query';

// Bad — modules are not on the root entry
import { useSession, useQuery, Router } from 'grainlet';
```

Not React: no `useState` / `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default. Signals are accessors (`count()`). In JSX write `{count()}` — `grainlet-vite` wraps call expressions.
